{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu01", "cards": [{"id": "u3.t.microorganism", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">mi<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">cro<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">OR<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gan<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ism<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"microorganism\" data-audio=\"audio/microorganism.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: microorganism\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-microorganism.webp\" width=\"448\" height=\"448\" alt=\"Colonies of bacteria on an agar plate. Each dot holds millions of cells too small to see one by one.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Colonies of bacteria on an agar plate. Each dot holds millions of cells too small to see one by one.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">琼脂平板上的细菌菌落。每个小点里有数百万个单独看不见的细胞。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agar_plate_with_colonies_square.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"microorganism\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Naked eye<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"8.834586466165414\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">an ant, about 2 mm,<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">is visible<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Microscope<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bacteria, a few<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">micrometres, need<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">it<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A living thing too small to see without a microscope.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>微生物<\/b>：小到不用显微镜就看不见的生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">micro = small, organism = living thing.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">micro = 小，organism = 生物。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Can you see a single bacterium without a microscope?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. It is only a few micrometres long.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.virus", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">VI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">rus<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"virus\" data-audio=\"audio/virus.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: virus\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-virus.webp\" width=\"700\" height=\"490\" alt=\"Rubella viruses under an electron microscope. Each round particle is about 60 nanometres across.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Rubella viruses under an electron microscope. Each round particle is about 60 nanometres across.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">电子显微镜下的风疹病毒。每个圆形颗粒直径约 60 纳米。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: CDC/Dr. Erskine Palmer · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubella_virus_TEM_B82-0203_lores.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"virus\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M100 22 L128 38 L128 70 L100 86 L72 70 L72 38 Z\" class=\"f2 k\"/><path d=\"M90 50 Q100 40 110 52 Q100 68 90 62\" class=\"f4\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"22\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"12\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"32\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"62\" y2=\"32\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"76\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"62\" y2=\"76\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"96\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">spikes<\/text><line x1=\"148\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"33\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"6.845238095238095\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">protein coat<\/text><line x1=\"148.0\" y1=\"50.0\" x2=\"128.0\" y2=\"52.0\"/><polygon points=\"128.0,52.0 132.3,49.4 132.7,53.7\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"8.214285714285714\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">RNA or DNA<\/text><line x1=\"148.0\" y1=\"72.0\" x2=\"111.0\" y2=\"58.0\"/><polygon points=\"111.0,58.0 116.0,57.6 114.4,61.6\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A tiny particle of genetic material inside a protein coat that can only reproduce inside a host cell.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>病毒<\/b>：蛋白质外壳包着遗传物质的微小颗粒，只能在宿主细胞内繁殖。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">virus = Latin for poison.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">virus 在拉丁语里是「毒」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Can a virus reproduce on its own?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. It needs a host cell.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.capsid", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">CAP<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">sid<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"capsid\" data-audio=\"audio/capsid.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: capsid\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"capsid\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M100 22 L128 38 L128 70 L100 86 L72 70 L72 38 Z\" class=\"f2 k\"/><path d=\"M90 50 Q100 40 110 52 Q100 68 90 62\" class=\"f4\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"22\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"12\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"32\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"62\" y2=\"32\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"76\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"62\" y2=\"76\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"96\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">capsid<\/text><line x1=\"158.0\" y1=\"52.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"54.0\"/><polygon points=\"130.0,54.0 134.3,51.5 134.6,55.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">The protein coat that surrounds and protects a virus&#x27;s genetic material.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>衣壳<\/b>：包围并保护病毒遗传物质的蛋白质外壳。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">capsid ~ capsule: a protein box.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">capsid 像个「蛋白质盒子」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is a capsid made of?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Protein.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.viral-envelope", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">VI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ral<\/span> <span class=\"st\">EN<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ve<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">lope<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"viral envelope\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: viral envelope\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"viral envelope\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" r=\"40\" class=\"f6 k\"/><path d=\"M100 40 L120 48 L120 72 L100 80 L80 72 L80 48 Z\" class=\"f2\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"10\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"26\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"64\" y2=\"26\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"60\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"60\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">envelope = membrane from the host<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An outer membrane some viruses take from the host cell, studded with spikes.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>病毒包膜<\/b>：部分病毒从宿主细胞获得的外层膜，上面有刺突。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">envelope = the wrapper around a letter.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">envelope = 信封：包在外面的一层。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Where does a viral envelope come from?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">From the host cell&#x27;s membrane.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.host-cell", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">HOST<\/span> <span class=\"st\">CELL<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"host cell\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: host cell\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"host cell\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"130\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"40\" class=\"f1 k\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"60\" r=\"12\" class=\"f4\"/><path d=\"M20 40 L40 40 L48 55 L40 70 L20 70 L12 55 Z\" class=\"f2 k\"/><line x1=\"52.0\" y1=\"55.0\" x2=\"80.0\" y2=\"55.0\"/><polygon points=\"80.0,55.0 75.5,57.2 75.5,52.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">the virus uses the host&#x27;s machinery<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">The living cell a virus enters and uses to make more viruses.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>宿主细胞<\/b>：病毒进入并利用来制造更多病毒的活细胞。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">host = the one who &quot;hosts&quot; a guest.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">host = 接待客人的主人。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why does a virus need a host cell?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">It has no machinery of its own to make proteins and copy itself.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.obligate-parasite", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">OB<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">li<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gate<\/span> <span class=\"st\">PAR<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">a<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">site<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"obligate parasite\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: obligate parasite\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"obligate parasite\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"46.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Outside<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">a cell:<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">no<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"80.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">activity<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Enters a<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">host<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">cell<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Copies<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">itself<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An organism that cannot survive or reproduce without living in or on a host.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>专性寄生物<\/b>：离开宿主就无法生存或繁殖的寄生生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">obligate = obliged, forced. They must have a host.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">obligate = 非如此不可。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why are viruses called obligate parasites?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">They can reproduce only inside a host cell.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.bacteriophage", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">bac<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TE<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ri<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">phage<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"bacteriophage\" data-audio=\"audio/bacteriophage.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: bacteriophage\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-bacteriophage.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"399\" alt=\"Left: clear spots on a plate where phages killed the bacteria. Right: phages under an electron microscope (bar = 200 nanometres).\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Left: clear spots on a plate where phages killed the bacteria. Right: phages under an electron microscope (bar = 200 nanometres).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">左：噬菌体杀死细菌后在平板上留下的透明斑。右：电子显微镜下的噬菌体（比例尺 = 200 纳米）。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Kornienko MA, Malakhova MV, Bespiatykh DA, Manuvera VA, Selezneva OV, Veselovsky VA … · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY 4.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bacteriophage_vB_KpnP_Klyazma.png\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"bacteriophage\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M85 18 L115 18 L125 36 L115 54 L85 54 L75 36 Z\" class=\"f2 k\"/><path d=\"M92 30 Q100 24 108 32 Q100 44 92 38\" class=\"f4\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"86\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"82\" y2=\"102\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"118\" y2=\"102\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"104\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"135\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">head (DNA)<\/text><line x1=\"133.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"34.0\"/><polygon points=\"120.0,34.0 123.2,30.1 125.0,34.1\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">tail<\/text><text x=\"125\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">tail fibres<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A virus that infects bacteria.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>噬菌体<\/b>：专门感染细菌的病毒。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">bacterio- = bacteria, -phage = eater. Bacteria eater.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">bacterio- = 细菌，-phage = 吞食。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does a bacteriophage infect?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Bacteria.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.lytic-cycle", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">LYT<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ic<\/span> <span class=\"st\">CY<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">cle<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"lytic cycle\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: lytic cycle\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"lytic cycle\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"38\"/><polygon points=\"149.0,36.3 137.8,35.3 143.0,26.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><polygon points=\"138.7,90.0 144.6,80.5 149.9,89.0\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><polygon points=\"51.0,83.7 62.2,84.7 57.0,93.2\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><polygon points=\"61.3,30.0 55.4,39.5 50.1,31.0\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"8\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"24.8\" font-size=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Attach<\/text><rect x=\"132\" y=\"46\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Inject DNA<\/text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"84\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"96.2\" font-size=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Make new<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"105.4\" font-size=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">viruses<\/text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"46\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f4\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Cell bursts<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A virus cycle in which the virus copies itself fast and bursts the host cell.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>裂解周期<\/b>：病毒迅速复制并使宿主细胞破裂的循环。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">lysis = splitting open. Lytic = bursts the cell.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">lysis = 裂开。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What happens to the host cell at the end of the lytic cycle?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">It bursts (lyses) and releases new viruses.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u3.t.microorganism", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A living thing too small to see without a microscope.”<\/i>", "opts": ["anaerobic", "bacteriophage", "nucleoid", "microorganism"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>microorganism<\/b>: A living thing too small to see without a microscope. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">微生物<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.virus", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A tiny particle of genetic material inside a protein coat that can only reproduce inside a host cell.”<\/i>", "opts": ["virus", "microorganism", "plasmid", "nucleoid"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>virus<\/b>: A tiny particle of genetic material inside a protein coat that can only reproduce inside a host cell. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">病毒<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.capsid", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“The protein coat that surrounds and protects a virus&#x27;s genetic material.”<\/i>", "opts": ["antibiotic", "capsid", "pathogen", "ribosome"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>capsid<\/b>: The protein coat that surrounds and protects a virus&#x27;s genetic material. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">衣壳<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.viral-envelope", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An outer membrane some viruses take from the host cell, studded with spikes.”<\/i>", "opts": ["pilus", "binary fission", "viral envelope", "mutualism"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>viral envelope<\/b>: An outer membrane some viruses take from the host cell, studded with spikes. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">病毒包膜<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.host-cell", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“The living cell a virus enters and uses to make more viruses.”<\/i>", "opts": ["microbiome", "host cell", "vaccine", "capsule"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>host cell<\/b>: The living cell a virus enters and uses to make more viruses. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">宿主细胞<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.obligate-parasite", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An organism that cannot survive or reproduce without living in or on a host.”<\/i>", "opts": ["microbiome", "thermophile", "binary fission", "obligate parasite"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>obligate parasite<\/b>: An organism that cannot survive or reproduce without living in or on a host. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">专性寄生物<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.bacteriophage", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A virus that infects bacteria.”<\/i>", "opts": ["bacteriophage", "pilus", "anaerobic", "nucleoid"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>bacteriophage<\/b>: A virus that infects bacteria. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">噬菌体<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.lytic-cycle", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A virus cycle in which the virus copies itself fast and bursts the host cell.”<\/i>", "opts": ["lytic cycle", "decomposer", "lysogenic cycle", "spirillum"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>lytic cycle<\/b>: A virus cycle in which the virus copies itself fast and bursts the host cell. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">裂解周期<\/span>", "whys": null}]}